{"id":"mahabharata-13-026","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":26,"title":"षड्विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 26 · The holy places","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks for the merit of seeing, bathing at and hearing of holy places, and Bhishma gives the teaching the sage Angiras gave to Gautama. It lists many tirthas, and the fruit of bathing there, such as for the one who bathes in a great lake and fasts for a month attaining the state of Jamadagni.","kn":"ತೀರ್ಥ ದರ್ಶನ, ಸ್ನಾನ, ಶ್ರವಣದ ಫಲ ಹೇಳಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅಂಗಿರಸ ಗೌತಮನಿಗೆ ನೀಡಿದ ಬೋಧನೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅನೇಕ ತೀರ್ಥಗಳು, ಅಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ನಾನದ ಫಲ, ಮಹಾಸರೋವರದಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ನಾನ ಮಾಡಿ ತಿಂಗಳು ಉಪವಾಸ ಮಾಡಿದವನಿಗೆ ಜಮದಗ್ನಿ ಗತಿ ಮೊದಲಾದುವನ್ನು ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर तीर्थों के दर्शन, स्नान और श्रवण का फल पूछते हैं, और भीष्म अंगिरा द्वारा गौतम को दिया उपदेश सुनाते हैं। उसमें अनेक तीर्थ और वहाँ स्नान के फल गिनाए गए हैं, जैसे महाह्रद में स्नान और एक मास उपवास से जमदग्नि की गति।","te":"తీర్థాల దర్శనం, స్నానం, శ్రవణం ఫలం చెప్పమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; అంగిరసుడు గౌతమునికి ఇచ్చిన బోధను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. అనేక తీర్థాలు, అక్కడ స్నాన ఫలాలు, మహాహ్రదంలో స్నానం చేసి నెల ఉపవసించినవాడు జమదగ్ని గతి పొందడం వంటివి పట్టిక చేస్తాడు.","ta":"தீர்த்தங்களைக் காண்பது, நீராடுவது, கேட்பதன் பலனை யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, அங்கிரஸ் கௌதமருக்குச் செய்த போதனையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். பல தீர்த்தங்களையும் அங்கு நீராடும் பலனையும், பெருங்குளத்தில் நீராடி ஒரு மாதம் உண்ணாநோன்பிருப்பவன் ஜமதக்னியின் நிலை பெறுவதையும் பட்டியலிடுகிறார்.","ml":"പുണ്യസ്ഥലങ്ങൾ കാണുന്നതിനും അവിടെ സ്നാനം ചെയ്യുന്നതിനും കേൾക്കുന്നതിനും ഉള്ള പുണ്യമെന്തെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. അംഗിരസ് മുനി ഗൗതമനോട് പറഞ്ഞ ഉപദേശം ഭീഷ്മർ നൽകുന്നു. അതിൽ പല തീർത്ഥങ്ങളും, അവിടെ സ്നാനം ചെയ്യുന്നതിന്റെ ഫലവും പറയുന്നു; മഹാതടാകത്തിൽ സ്നാനം ചെയ്ത് ഒരു മാസം ഉപവസിക്കുന്നവൻ ജമദഗ്നിയുടെ പദവി നേടുമെന്നും പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.26; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तीर्थानां दर्शनं श्रेयः स्नानं च भरतर्षभ ।\nश्रवणं च महाप्राज्ञ श्रोतुमिच्छामि तत्त्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull of the Bharatas, visiting holy places, bathing in them and hearing about them is good. Wise one, I wish to hear about these truly."}},{"n":2,"text":"पृथिव्यां यानि तीर्थानि पुण्यानि भरतर्षभ ।\nवक्तुमर्हसि मे तानि श्रोतास्मि नियतः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, you should tell me about the holy and meritorious places on earth; lord, I will listen with discipline."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"इममङ्गिरसा प्रोक्तं तीर्थवंशं महाद्युते ।\nश्रोतुमर्हसि भद्रं ते प्राप्स्यसे धर्ममुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radiant one, you should hear this lineage of holy places spoken by Angiras; may you be blessed and gain the highest dharma."}},{"n":4,"text":"तपोवनगतं विप्रमभिगम्य महामुनिम् ।\nपप्रच्छाङ्गिरसं वीर गौतमः संशितव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero Gautama, firm in his vows, went to the great sage Angiras, a brahmin in the forest of austerities, and asked him."}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्ति मे भगवन्कश्चित्तीर्थेभ्यो धर्मसंशयः ।\nतत्सर्वं श्रोतुमिच्छामि तन्मे शंस महामुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Blessed one, I have a doubt about dharma concerning holy places. I wish to hear all of that; tell me, great sage."}},{"n":6,"text":"उपस्पृश्य फलं किं स्यात्तेषु तीर्थेषु वै मुने ।\nप्रेत्यभावे महाप्राज्ञ तद्यथास्ति तथा वद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sage, what fruit comes from bathing in those holy places, in the next life? Wise one, tell it as it is.'"}},{"text":"अङ्गिरा उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Angiras said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"सप्ताहं चन्द्रभागां वै वितस्तामूर्मिमालिनीम् ।\nविगाह्य वै निराहारो निर्ममो मुनिवद्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bathed for seven days in the Chandrabhaga and the wave-garlanded Vitasta, fasting and without possessiveness, one becomes like a sage."}},{"n":8,"text":"काश्मीरमण्डले नद्यो याः पतन्ति महानदम् ।\nता नदीः सिन्धुमासाद्य शीलवान्स्वर्गमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the Kashmir region, the rivers that fall into the great river: reaching those rivers and the Sindhu, a virtuous man would obtain heaven."}},{"n":9,"text":"पुष्करं च प्रभासं च नैमिषं सागरोदकम् ।\nदेविकामिन्द्रमार्गं च स्वर्णबिन्दुं विगाह्य च ।\nविबोध्यते विमानस्थः सोऽप्सरोभिरभिष्टुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bathed in Pushkara, Prabhasa, Naimisha, the sea waters, the Devika, Indramarga and Svarnabindu, one is woken in a celestial car and praised by apsaras."}},{"n":10,"text":"हिरण्यबिन्दुं विक्षोभ्य प्रयतश्चाभिवाद्य तम् ।\nकुशेशयं च देवत्वं पूयते तस्य किल्बिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having plunged into Hiranyabindu, and saluted it with discipline, and at Kusheshaya, one gains godhood and one's sin is cleansed."}},{"n":11,"text":"इन्द्रतोयां समासाद्य गन्धमादनसंनिधौ ।\nकरतोयां कुरङ्गेषु त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति विगाह्य नियतः शुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who, pure and restrained, bathes at Indratoya near Gandhamadana and at Karatoya among the Kurangas after fasting three nights obtains the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":12,"text":"गङ्गाद्वारे कुशावर्ते बिल्वके नेमिपर्वते ।\nतथा कनखले स्नात्वा धूतपाप्मा दिवं व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Gangadvara, Kushavarta, Bilvaka, Nemiparvata and Kanakhala, one is rid of sin and goes to heaven."}},{"n":13,"text":"अपां ह्रद उपस्पृश्य वाजपेयफलं लभेत् ।\nब्रह्मचारी जितक्रोधः सत्यसंधस्त्वहिंसकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing in the Apah pool, one who is celibate, has conquered anger, is true to his word and non-violent gains the fruit of the Vajapeya."}},{"n":14,"text":"यत्र भागीरथी गङ्गा भजते दिशमुत्तराम् ।\nमहेश्वरस्य निष्ठाने यो नरस्त्वभिषिच्यते ।\nएकमासं निराहारः स्वयं पश्यति देवताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the Ganga, Bhagirathi, turns to the northern direction, a man who is bathed at the place of Maheshvara and fasts a month sees the gods himself."}},{"n":15,"text":"सप्तगङ्गे त्रिगङ्गे च इन्द्रमार्गे च तर्पयन् ।\nसुधां वै लभते भोक्तुं यो नरो जायते पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Offering water at Saptaganga, Triganga and Indramarga, a man who is reborn gets nectar to eat."}},{"n":16,"text":"महाश्रम उपस्पृश्य योऽग्निहोत्रपरः शुचिः ।\nएकमासं निराहारः सिद्धिं मासेन स व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who bathes at Mahashrama, pure and devoted to the fire offering, fasting a month, attains perfection within a month."}},{"n":17,"text":"महाह्रद उपस्पृश्य भृगुतुङ्गे त्वलोलुपः ।\nत्रिरात्रोपोषितो भूत्वा मुच्यते ब्रह्महत्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Mahahrada, free from greed at Bhrigutunga and fasting for three nights, one is freed from the sin of killing a brahmin."}},{"n":18,"text":"कन्याकूप उपस्पृश्य बलाकायां कृतोदकः ।\nदेवेषु कीर्तिं लभते यशसा च विराजते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bathed at Kanyakupa and offered water at Balaka, one gains fame among the gods and shines with renown."}},{"n":19,"text":"देशकाल उपस्पृश्य तथा सुन्दरिकाह्रदे ।\nअश्विभ्यां रूपवर्चस्यं प्रेत्य वै लभते नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Deshakala and at the Sundarika pool, a man gains, in the next world, the beauty and radiance of the Ashvins."}},{"n":20,"text":"महागङ्गामुपस्पृश्य कृत्तिकाङ्गारके तथा ।\nपक्षमेकं निराहारः स्वर्गमाप्नोति निर्मलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bathed in the Mahaganga and at Krittikangaraka, fasting for a fortnight, one becomes stainless and reaches heaven."}},{"n":21,"text":"वैमानिक उपस्पृश्य किङ्किणीकाश्रमे तथा ।\nनिवासेऽप्सरसां दिव्ये कामचारी महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Vaimanika and the Kinkinika hermitage, one is honored, moving at will in the divine abode of the apsaras."}},{"n":22,"text":"कालिकाश्रममासाद्य विपाशायां कृतोदकः ।\nब्रह्मचारी जितक्रोधस्त्रिरात्रान्मुच्यते भवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the Kalika hermitage and offering water in the Vipasha, a celibate who has conquered anger is freed from worldly existence in three nights."}},{"n":23,"text":"आश्रमे कृत्तिकानां तु स्नात्वा यस्तर्पयेत्पितॄन् ।\nतोषयित्वा महादेवं निर्मलः स्वर्गमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who bathes at the hermitage of the Krittikas and offers to the ancestors, and pleases Mahadeva, becomes stainless and reaches heaven."}},{"n":24,"text":"महापुर उपस्पृश्य त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nत्रसानां स्थावराणां च द्विपदानां भयं त्यजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who bathes at Mahapura and fasts three nights leaves fear of moving and unmoving beings and of two-footed ones."}},{"n":25,"text":"देवदारुवने स्नात्वा धूतपाप्मा कृतोदकः ।\nदेवलोकमवाप्नोति सप्तरात्रोषितः शुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing in the Devadaru forest, rid of sin, offering water and staying seven nights pure, one attains the world of the gods."}},{"n":26,"text":"कौशन्ते च कुशस्तम्बे द्रोणशर्मपदे तथा ।\nआपःप्रपतने स्नातः सेव्यते सोऽप्सरोगणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Kaushanta, Kushastamba, Dronasharmapada and Apahprapatana, one is served by hosts of apsaras."}},{"n":27,"text":"चित्रकूटे जनस्थाने तथा मन्दाकिनीजले ।\nविगाह्य वै निराहारो राजलक्ष्मीं निगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Plunging into Chitrakuta, Janasthana and the waters of the Mandakini while fasting, one gains royal fortune."}},{"n":28,"text":"श्यामायास्त्वाश्रमं गत्वा उष्य चैवाभिषिच्य च ।\nत्रींस्त्रिरात्रान्स संधाय गन्धर्वनगरे वसेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gone to the hermitage of Shyama, stayed there and bathed, and keeping to three periods of three nights, one dwells in the city of the gandharvas."}},{"n":29,"text":"रमण्यां च उपस्पृश्य तथा वै गन्धतारिके ।\nएकमासं निराहारस्त्वन्तर्धानफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Ramani and at Gandhatarika and fasting for a month, one obtains the fruit of invisibility."}},{"n":30,"text":"कौशिकीद्वारमासाद्य वायुभक्षस्त्वलोलुपः ।\nएकविंशतिरात्रेण स्वर्गमारोहते नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Kaushikidvara, living on air and without greed, a man ascends to heaven in twenty-one nights."}},{"n":31,"text":"मतङ्गवाप्यां यः स्नायादेकरात्रेण सिध्यति ।\nविगाहति ह्यनालम्बमन्धकं वै सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who bathes in the Matangavapi attains success in one night; he plunges into the eternal, supportless darkness."}},{"n":32,"text":"नैमिषे स्वर्गतीर्थे च उपस्पृश्य जितेन्द्रियः ।\nफलं पुरुषमेधस्य लभेन्मासं कृतोदकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bathed at Naimisha and Svargatirtha with senses controlled and offering water for a month, one obtains the fruit of the human sacrifice."}},{"n":33,"text":"गङ्गाह्रद उपस्पृश्य तथा चैवोत्पलावने ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति तत्र मासं कृतोदकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Gangahrada and in the Utpalavana and offering water there for a month, one obtains the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":34,"text":"गङ्गायमुनयोस्तीर्थे तथा कालंजरे गिरौ ।\nषष्टिह्रद उपस्पृश्य दानं नान्यद्विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the confluence of the Ganga and Yamuna, at the hill Kalanjara, and bathing at Shashtihrada, no other gift is greater."}},{"n":35,"text":"दश तीर्थसहस्राणि तिस्रः कोट्यस्तथापराः ।\nसमागच्छन्ति माघ्यां तु प्रयागे भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ten thousand holy places and three crores more, bull of the Bharatas, gather at Prayaga in the month of Magha."}},{"n":36,"text":"माघमासं प्रयागे तु नियतः संशितव्रतः ।\nस्नात्वा तु भरतश्रेष्ठ निर्मलः स्वर्गमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, one who, disciplined and firm in vows, bathes at Prayaga in the month of Magha becomes stainless and reaches heaven."}},{"n":37,"text":"मरुद्गण उपस्पृश्य पितॄणामाश्रमे शुचिः ।\nवैवस्वतस्य तीर्थे च तीर्थभूतो भवेन्नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing, pure, at Marudgana and the hermitage of the ancestors, and at Vaivasvata's ford, a man becomes himself a holy place."}},{"n":38,"text":"तथा ब्रह्मशिरो गत्वा भागीरथ्यां कृतोदकः ।\nएकमासं निराहारः सोमलोकमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gone to Brahmashiras and offered water in the Bhagirathi, fasting a month, one would reach the Moon's world."}},{"n":39,"text":"कपोतके नरः स्नात्वा अष्टावक्रे कृतोदकः ।\nद्वादशाहं निराहारो नरमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who bathes at Kapotaka and offers water at Ashtavakra, fasting twelve days, gains the fruit of the human sacrifice."}},{"n":40,"text":"मुञ्जपृष्ठं गयां चैव निरृतिं देवपर्वतम् ।\nतृतीयां क्रौञ्चपादीं च ब्रह्महत्या विशुध्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Munjaprishtha, Gaya, Nirriti, Devaparvata and the third Kraunchapadi, one is purified from killing a brahmin."}},{"n":41,"text":"कलश्यां वाप्युपस्पृश्य वेद्यां च बहुशोजलाम् ।\nअग्नेः पुरे नरः स्नात्वा विशालायां कृतोदकः ।\nदेवह्रद उपस्पृश्य ब्रह्मभूतो विराजते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Kalashi, the Vedi with its abundant waters, and at Agnipura, offering water at Vishala and bathing at Devahrada, one shines as one who has become Brahman."}},{"n":42,"text":"पुरापवर्तनं नन्दां महानन्दां च सेव्य वै ।\nनन्दने सेव्यते दान्तस्त्वप्सरोभिरहिंसकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having served Purapavartana, Nanda and Mahananda, a disciplined, non-violent man is attended by apsaras in Nandana."}},{"n":43,"text":"उर्वशीकृत्तिकायोगे गत्वा यः सुसमाहितः ।\nलौहित्ये विधिवत्स्नात्वा पुण्डरीकफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man of fully concentrated mind who goes at the conjunction of Urvashi and Krittika and bathes properly in the Lauhitya gains the fruit of the Pundarika."}},{"n":44,"text":"रामह्रद उपस्पृश्य विशालायां कृतोदकः ।\nद्वादशाहं निराहारः कल्मषाद्विप्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Ramahrada and offering water at Vishala, fasting twelve days, one is freed of impurity."}},{"n":45,"text":"महाह्रद उपस्पृश्य शुद्धेन मनसा नरः ।\nएकमासं निराहारो जमदग्निगतिं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man of pure mind who bathes at Mahahrada and fasts a month reaches the state of Jamadagni."}},{"n":46,"text":"विन्ध्ये संताप्य चात्मानं सत्यसंधस्त्वहिंसकः ।\nषण्मासं पदमास्थाय मासेनैकेन शुध्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who heats himself in the Vindhya, true to his word and non-violent, standing on his foot for six months, is purified in a single month."}},{"n":47,"text":"नर्मदायामुपस्पृश्य तथा सूर्पारकोदके ।\nएकपक्षं निराहारो राजपुत्रो विधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing in the Narmada and in the waters of Surparaka, fasting for a fortnight, one is ordained a king's son."}},{"n":48,"text":"जम्बूमार्गे त्रिभिर्मासैः संयतः सुसमाहितः ।\nअहोरात्रेण चैकेन सिद्धिं समधिगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Jambumarga, one who is controlled and fully concentrated reaches success in three months, or in one day and night."}},{"n":49,"text":"कोकामुखे विगाह्यापो गत्वा चण्डालिकाश्रमम् ।\nशाकभक्षश्चीरवासाः कुमारीर्विन्दते दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Plunging into the waters at Kokamukha and going to Chandalika's hermitage, eating vegetables and wearing bark, one wins ten maidens."}},{"n":50,"text":"वैवस्वतस्य सदनं न स गच्छेत्कदाचन ।\nयस्य कन्याह्रदे वासो देवलोकं स गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He would never go to the house of Vaivasvata; one who lives at Kanyahrada goes to the world of the gods."}},{"n":51,"text":"प्रभासे त्वेकरात्रेण अमावास्यां समाहितः ।\nसिध्यतेऽत्र महाबाहो यो नरो जायते पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Prabhasa, one who is concentrated at the new moon, in one night, attains success here, and is not born again, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":52,"text":"उज्जानक उपस्पृश्य आर्ष्टिषेणस्य चाश्रमे ।\nपिङ्गायाश्चाश्रमे स्नात्वा सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Ujjanaka, at the hermitage of Arshtishena and at the hermitage of Pingala, one is freed from all sins."}},{"n":53,"text":"कुल्यायां समुपस्पृश्य जप्त्वा चैवाघमर्षणम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति त्रिरात्रोपोषितः शुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Kulya and reciting the Aghamarshana, pure and fasting three nights, one obtains the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":54,"text":"पिण्डारक उपस्पृश्य एकरात्रोषितो नरः ।\nअग्निष्टोममवाप्नोति प्रभातां शर्वरीं शुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who bathes at Pindaraka, staying one night, pure, obtains the Agnishtoma by the following dawn."}},{"n":55,"text":"तथा ब्रह्मसरो गत्वा धर्मारण्योपशोभितम् ।\nपुण्डरीकमवाप्नोति प्रभातां शर्वरीं शुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Brahmasaras adorned with Dharmaranya, pure, one obtains the Pundarika by the following dawn."}},{"n":56,"text":"मैनाके पर्वते स्नात्वा तथा संध्यामुपास्य च ।\nकामं जित्वा च वै मासं सर्वमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at the mountain Mainaka and worshipping at twilight, one conquers desire and in a month gains the fruit of the Sarvamedha."}},{"n":57,"text":"विख्यातो हिमवान्पुण्यः शंकरश्वशुरो गिरिः ।\nआकरः सर्वरत्नानां सिद्धचारणसेवितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The famed holy Himalaya, father-in-law of Shankara, mountain and mine of all jewels, served by siddhas and charanas, is there."}},{"n":58,"text":"शरीरमुत्सृजेत्तत्र विधिपूर्वमनाशके ।\nअध्रुवं जीवितं ज्ञात्वा यो वै वेदान्तगो द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who has mastered the Vedanta and knows life is uncertain may give up his body there by fasting according to rule."}},{"n":59,"text":"अभ्यर्च्य देवतास्तत्र नमस्कृत्य मुनींस्तथा ।\nततः सिद्धो दिवं गच्छेद्ब्रह्मलोकं सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having worshipped the gods there and saluted the sages, the perfected one then goes to heaven, the eternal world of Brahma."}},{"n":60,"text":"कामं क्रोधं च लोभं च यो जित्वा तीर्थमावसेत् ।\nन तेन किंचिन्न प्राप्तं तीर्थाभिगमनाद्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who stays at a holy place after conquering desire, anger and greed lacks nothing; nothing is unobtained by visiting holy places."}},{"n":61,"text":"यान्यगम्यानि तीर्थानि दुर्गाणि विषमाणि च ।\nमनसा तानि गम्यानि सर्वतीर्थसमासतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those holy places that are unreachable, difficult or rough should be visited by the mind; so it is in sum for all holy places."}},{"n":62,"text":"इदं मेध्यमिदं धन्यमिदं स्वर्ग्यमिदं सुखम् ।\nइदं रहस्यं देवानामाप्लाव्यानां च पावनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is purifying, auspicious, heavenly and happy; this is a secret of the gods and purifies those who bathe."}},{"n":63,"text":"इदं दद्याद्द्विजातीनां साधूनामात्मजस्य वा ।\nसुहृदां च जपेत्कर्णे शिष्यस्यानुगतस्य वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should give this to the twice-born, to good people or to one's son, or whisper it in the ear of friends or a devoted disciple."}},{"n":64,"text":"दत्तवान्गौतमस्येदमङ्गिरा वै महातपाः ।\nगुरुभिः समनुज्ञातः काश्यपेन च धीमता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angiras of great austerity gave this to Gautama, permitted by his teachers and by the wise Kashyapa."}},{"n":65,"text":"महर्षीणामिदं जप्यं पावनानां तथोत्तमम् ।\nजपंश्चाभ्युत्थितः शश्वन्निर्मलः स्वर्गमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the best recitation, purifying the great sages. One who recites it, rising constantly, becomes stainless and reaches heaven."}},{"n":66,"text":"इदं यश्चापि शृणुयाद्रहस्यं त्वङ्गिरोमतम् ।\nउत्तमे च कुले जन्म लभेज्जातिं च संस्मरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who hears this secret doctrine of Angiras obtains birth in a noble family and remembers his past birth."}}]}]}